to be a feature not just of high-\(p_{T}\) trigger-and-associated correlations but also of low-\(p_{T}\) correlations using particles restricted to \(p_{T}<2.0\) GeV. Numerous hypotheses were put forth to explain its appearance in heavy ion collisions:

* coupling to longitudinal flow of induced radiation of energetic partons propagating through the medium [19];
* color field turbulence [20];
* anisotropic plasma [21];
* jet-quenching combined with strong radial flow [22];
